  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/Freeze late tonight into early Sunday \nmorning \n\nA noticeably cooler northerly breeze, expansive cloud cover, and\nspotty light precip this morning eventually gives way to \nclearing skies and diminishing wind by tonight as high pressure \nslides eastward from the Ohio Valley. This sets up favorable \nconditions for a widespread frost/freeze overnight into early \nSunday morning with the coldest min temps in the 25-30F range.\nThe overnight frost/freeze risk will continue for portions of\nCPA into next week. \n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry weather next week\n\nHigh pressure anchored on the northwest side of developing\nNor'easter off the NC coast will provide another extended\nstretch of dry weather in CPA Sunday through next week. This\npattern will feature seasonably warm days, chilly nights, and\nlow humidity.",
